  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the project instructions and OpenSocrates controller, then build the app and verify it through the API, browser, restart, and a repeatable load run.",
    "I’m using Python’s standard-library HTTP server with SQLite. SQLite gives the stock and order operations a durable transaction boundary, and the stack needs no package download or external service. I’ll build the routes and data model first, then connect the UI and run end-to-end checks.",
    "The backend and UI are in place. I’m checking the failure paths now: rejected reservations must leave every line unchanged, retries must replay exactly once, and restart must preserve both stock and the retry record.",
    "The API test suite passes, including concurrent reservation, replay, isolation, validation, returns, and restart checks. The browser workflow also passes from login through a full return; its first run exposed a test timing issue after a partial return, which I corrected by waiting for the updated order version. I’m inspecting the UI captures and then measuring a repeatable local workload.",
    "The 8-client load run found intermittent read transport errors while all write workflows completed. I’m checking the server’s connection handling and will keep the failed run in the verification record; the performance result should reflect the final rerun, not hide this finding.",
    "The connection backlog change removed the intermittent read errors in repeated 8-client runs. I also tightened order pagination so later pages keep the original set of matching order IDs, even if an order changes status between requests. The route tests now cover that case. I’m recording the setup, architecture, and measured results in the deliverables.",
    "DepotFlow is complete and locally runnable. Start it with `PORT=8000 DATA_DIR=./data SEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh`. The [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md) covers demo accounts and setup; [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md) describes the transaction and isolation rules.\n\nThe API and restart integration suite passed. The browser exercise passed order creation through full return, audit, search, admin stock adjustment, and south-viewer isolation, with zero page errors. The final local load run recorded 300 reads and 240 writes with zero errors; results and limitations are in [verification.md](<CELL>/workspace/verification.md).\n\nPython and SQLite satisfy the required local, durable, atomic workflow without external services. The accepted tradeoff is a single SQLite writer; the short loopback load run does not establish sustained capacity. OpenSocrates native activation is unconfirmed; its installed trade-off procedure was read and used for the stack choice.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
